  - "Most people picture therapy as a toolbox: the right technique for the right problem, applied by someone who knows which tool to grab. So here's the part that surprises people. The technique was never the medicine. You can feel the difference in the first five minutes, between a therapist who is listening to you and one who is quietly listening for the next technique to deploy."
  - "The change happens in the relationship, not in the toolkit. That isn't a soft or fuzzy claim; it's the most practical thing we know. When you feel truly understood by someone who also isn't afraid to challenge you, something loosens that no clever intervention can force. Everything else we do is built on top of that."
